  "id": "COMPOUND:40269 - PROTEIN:5865",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 3-(Methylthio)propyl acetate may interact with SK-VLB through a series of target relationships, primarily involving hepatocytes. The compound is linked to hepatocytes, which are then targeted by multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and Cocosamide B. These latter compounds are both targeted by SK-VLB, indicating a potential pathway where 3-(Methylthio)propyl acetate may influence SK-VLB through indirect interactions with hepatocytes. The evidence is consistent with a mechanism where the compound acts as a target for downstream molecules that ultimately affect SK-VLB. The integration of these relationships highlights a possible role for 3-(Methylthio)propyl acetate in modulating SK-VLB through a network of cellular targets, though the exact mechanism remains to be elucidated.",
